{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgBxHa16sSVJws5rVUAfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The main consumers are the chart's visit-related components and hooks: the banner tags, the visit actions menu, the end-visit dialog, the visit forms, and `usePatientChartPatientAndVisit`. Most of them read `activeVisit` or call `mutate`, so a change to `useVisit`'s return shape, caching, or revalidation would reach all of them. The test files mock `useVisit` and would need updating too.\n\n**Production call sites (most affected first)**\n\n1. `usePatientChartPatientAndVisit` calls `useVisit` for the active visit when there is no valid visit context, and relies on its `activeVisit` and `mutate`. It is the chart's main consumer.\n2. `VisitTag` (banner) reads `activeVisit` and `isLoading` to decide whether to show the \"Active Visit\" tag.\n3. `VisitAttributeTags` (banner) reads `activeVisit.attributes`.\n4. `StopVisitOverflowMenuItem` shows the \"End active visit\" item only when `activeVisit` is set.\n5. `DeleteVisitOverflowMenuItem` shows the \"Delete active visit\" item only when `activeVisit` is set.\n6. `EndVisitDialog` reads `activeVisit` and calls `mutate()` after ending the visit.\n7. `VisitForm` calls `mutate` from `useVisit` after a visit is started.\n8. `ExportedVisitForm` reads `activeVisit` and `isLoading` for the visit form.\n9. `useOptimisticVisitMutations` imports `useVisit` (its call sites are not in the lines I read). It also relies on the same SWR cache keys.\n10. `invalidateCurrentVisit` targets the SWR key that `useVisit` uses; its doc comment refers to `useVisit`.\n\n**Tests that mock `useVisit`** (they would break or go stale if the return shape changed)\n\n- `visit-attribute-tags.test.tsx`, `stop-visit.test.tsx`, `delete-visit.test.tsx`, `end-visit-dialog.test.tsx`, `visit-tag.test.tsx`, `visit-form.test.tsx`, `patient-chart.resources.test.tsx`, and `immunizations-detailed-summary.test.tsx`.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- The `useVisit` source is in `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useVisit.ts`. It returns `activeVisit`, `currentVisit`, `isLoading`, `isValidating`, `error`, and `mutate`, and it is backed by SWR keys under `/visit?patient=`.\n- Line ranges for the components are estimates from the lines I read. Where I did not see the end of a function, I used a nearby end line.\n- The core repository has `useVisit` mocks in `esm-react-utils/mock.tsx` and `mock-jest.tsx`. Those would need updating too, but they are not consumers.\n- I did not check the other 25 or so repositories in the org for `useVisit` usage, since the question is limited to the patient chart.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useVisit.ts\", \"startLine\": 52, \"endLine\": 142},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.ts\", \"startLine\": 73, \"endLine\": 94},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-banner-app/src/banner-tags/visit-tag.extension.tsx\", \"startLine\": 13, \"endLine\": 21},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-banner-tags/visit-attribute-tags.extension.tsx\", \"startLine\": 36, \"endLine\": 64},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/actions-buttons/stop-visit.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 16, \"endLine\": 37},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/actions-buttons/delete-visit.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 16, \"endLine\": 39},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visit-prompt/end-visit-dialog.modal.tsx\", \"startLine\": 20, \"endLine\": 82},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visit-form/visit-form.workspace.tsx\", \"startLine\": 32, \"endLine\": 66},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-pa